# Committed test fixtures are an intentional exception to the blanket *.safetensors rule above
# (they're tiny, hand-generated inputs the convert tests read at runtime, not model checkpoints).
!tests/convert/fixtures/*.safetensors

# tests/kernels/test_kernel_bandwidth.cpp's --capture golden (review finding, 2026-09-20): a
# ~19 MB binary, fully regenerable by `test_kernel_bandwidth --capture <path>` against the pre-P6
# kernel, and not meant to be a permanent artifact -- the repo now has a public remote (history was
# scrubbed 2026-09-20), so anything staged here lands in that history forever. The test itself
# SKIPs (CTest SKIPPED, not FAILED) with a regeneration hint when this file is absent, same
# convention tests/model's golden-data tests already use.
tests/kernels/golden/
